{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792229972,"nonce":"viXWuxaTAlFWbfcU1qBA1cTQfJ4=","title":"Python: `s - p` between two typed set shapes copies both into library sets","message":"typed = set([frozenset(x) for x in groups])    # Set(Set(Object, frozen))\n    def run(s, p, n):\n        for i in range(n):\n            k += len(s - p)                         # p: Set(Object, frozen)\n\nwith 39 frozensets of 1 to 10 tuples in `s` and one tuple in `p`: 20000 differences take 1.1 s on zypy (Mac, light build), 0.0068 s on CPython. The same with `s` a Set(Object) of boxed frozensets takes 0.022 s. The difference of two sets of different shapes goes through the set operation hooks, which copy both operands into the library's own set (rehashing every frozenset value) before operating.\n\nReproducer: hs6.py in the session scratch (rows, cols and diagonals of a 10x10 board as frozensets).","files":null}]}